# OVERDRIVE GAME OVER
# Game over: a slow falling jingle, held 16-bit piano chords, no drums. Plays once.
# OVERDRIVE, a suite for one game: TITLE, STAGE, BOSS, CALM, DUNGEON, VICTORY, GAME OVER and
# CREDITS. All in F# minor or its relative A major, on one set of instruments, so the cues
# sound like one game. The stage's chords, i - VI - III - VII, open the title too.
#
# A starting point made by PokeyTracker's New song window, by rule: each section's beat, bass
# and accompaniment worked out from the key, the chords and the band chosen. The tune is yours.
# Chords: i VII VI v:  F#m E D C#m.
# The format is in Demo1/CLAUDE.md, under "Song files".

song   OVERDRIVE GAME OVER
key    F# MINOR

# A plain square wave, for a tune.
instrument LEAD
  table      tone
  volume     12 11 10 10 9
  distortion tone
  release    2

# Distortion C, for a bass. Its table skips notes - see which in the tracker's colours.
instrument BASS
  table      buzz
  volume     12 11 10 9 8
  distortion buzz
  release    3

# A piano: struck, falling away, and holding softly - 16-bit, so every note is within two cents.
instrument PIANO
  table      wide
  volume     13 12 11 10 10 9 9 8 8 7 7 6 6 5 5 5 4 4 4 3
  distortion tone
  release    3

channel 1 notes LEAD
  note  Empty: the tune is yours.
  voice LEAD

channel 2 notes BASS
  note  Bass: roots, on the chords' roots.
  voice BASS
  track INTRO F#2 . . .  . . . .  F#2 . . .  . . . .
  track INTRO2 E2 . . .  . . . .  C#2 . . .  . . . .
  track END    F#2 . . .  . . . .  . . . .  . . . .

channel 3 pair LOW BYTE
  note  The low byte of channel 4's 16-bit divider.

channel 4 notes PATTERN
  note  Held chord, on each chord.
  voice PIANO
  track INTRO F#m . . .  . . . .  . . . .  . . . .
  track INTRO2 E . . .  . . . .  C#m . . .  . . . .
  track END    F#m . . .  . . . .  . . . .  . . . .

# The order list: a section at a time.
audctl $28
speed  10
section INTRO
line   .  INTRO  .  INTRO
line   .  INTRO2  .  INTRO2
section END
line   .  END  .  END
end
